-- title:
--   Local–global compatibility at a Taylor–Wiles prime, pointwise form
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and $p$ a prime lying in its maximal ideal. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $\mathrm{Res}(\mathcal O)$, i.e. a rank-two $\mathrm{Res}(\mathcal O)$-module with a $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$-action trivial on some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, and assume $\bar\rho$ becomes irreducible over $\overline{\mathrm{Res}(\mathcal O)}$. Let $N\neq 0$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathrm{Res}(\mathcal O)$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_{\Delta,j}\colon(\mathbb Z/q_j)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_j-1)}$ be homomorphisms and $\alpha_j\in\mathrm{Res}(\mathcal O)$; put $L=N(\prod_j q_j)r$, $H_R=\ker((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times)$ and $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker(\pi_{\Delta,j})_j$, and assume the commutation hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` for the operators and diamond operators on the corresponding cohomology carrier. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a second such discrete valuation ring, an $\mathcal O$-algebra via a local homomorphism, and let $\lambda$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism to $\mathcal O'$ from the Hecke ring `HeckeRing`, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of endomorphisms of the localised module generated by the Hecke and diamond operators. Fix $i$ with $p\mid q_i-1$, assume $\alpha_i^2-\theta(T_{q_i})\alpha_i+q_i=0$ and $2\alpha_i\neq\theta(T_{q_i})$, and let $\mathrm{cyc}$ be a homomorphism from the Galois group to $(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times$ with $\sigma\mu=\mu^{\mathrm{cyc}(\sigma)}$ for all $q_i$-th roots of unity $\mu$. Finally let $\rho$ be a Galois representation on a free $\mathcal O'$-module of rank two, adically continuous, whose trace at every Frobenius at a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\neq p$ equals $\lambda(T_\ell)$, and whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Then for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q_i$ is a non-unit there is an $\mathcal O'$-basis $b_0,b_1$ of the underlying module such that every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ fixes $b_1$ and satisfies $\rho(\sigma)b_0=\lambda(\langle u\rangle)\,b_0$ for every $u\in H_R$ whose image under $\pi_{\Delta,i}$ agrees with $\pi_{\Delta,i}(\mathrm{cyc}(\sigma))$ and whose images under the other $\pi_{\Delta,j}$ are trivial, and such that every Frobenius $\varphi$ at $q_i$ for $P$ satisfies $\rho(\varphi)b_1=a\,b_1$ for some $a\in\mathcal O'$ whose residue is the image of $\alpha_i$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility statement at a Taylor–Wiles prime $q_i$ in its pointwise form, for a discrete-valuation-ring valued point $\lambda$ of the Hecke ring of auxiliary level: inertia at $q_i$ acts in a suitable basis by $\mathrm{diag}(\lambda(\langle u\rangle),1)$, and Frobenius at $q_i$ preserves the inertia-fixed line with eigenvalue lifting $\alpha_i$. It is used to deduce the corresponding statement over the Hecke ring itself in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_basis_inertia_apply_eq_diamond_smul`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_basis_inertia_apply_eq_diamond_smul).
